=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# updates refusals ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: The refusals before asking, each from the stand-in$
# planner on the real reading: the direction, the host.$
$
# on, timer-off ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# apt-daily-upgrade.timer is off, and hardn leaves apt's timers$
# to you. Run systemctl enable --now apt-daily-upgrade.timer,$
# then try again.$
$
# on, masked ---------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# apt-daily-upgrade.service is masked, and hardn leaves apt's$
# timers to you. Run systemctl unmask apt-daily-upgrade.service,$
# then try again.$
$
# on, missing --------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# apt-daily-upgrade.service is missing. Reinstall apt, then try$
# again.$
$
# on, enable-off -----------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# APT::Periodic::Enable "0", in /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99site,$
# turns apt's daily jobs off. Remove that line, then try again.$
$
# on, no-origin ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# 50unattended-upgrades allows no origin, so nothing would be$
# upgraded. Add your distribution's origins there, then try$
# again.$
$
# on, extra-packages -------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Installing unattended-upgrades would also change other$
# packages: Inst libc6 [2.41-11] (2.41-12 Debian:13.1/stable$
# [arm64]). Install it by hand, then try again.$
$
# on, not-read -------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# apt can't read its settings: Syntax error$
# /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99site:1: Extra junk at end of file. Fix$
# that, then try again.$
$
# off, not-read ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# apt can't read its settings: Syntax error$
# /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99site:1: Extra junk at end of file. Fix$
# that, then try again.$
$
# off, edited --------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Not undone: /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52hardn-auto-upgrades changed$
# since hardn wrote it. Put it back as it was or undo the rest$
# by hand.$
$
# off, edited-alpine -------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Not undone: /etc/periodic/daily/apk changed since hardn$
# installed it. Put it back as it was or undo the rest by hand.$
$
# off, no-record -----------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Updates stay on without hardn's file: 20auto-upgrades turns$
# them on, and hardn has no record that it installed unattended-$
# upgrades. Turn them off by hand.$
$
# on, pve9 -----------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Nothing needs changing.$
$
# off, debian13 ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Nothing to undo: hardn did not turn this on. Turn it off by$
# hand.$
$
# on, by-hardn-debian ------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Nothing needs changing.$
$
# on, own-file -------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Nothing needs changing.$
$
$

